{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>At the mouth of HaShem the children of Israel journeyed, and at the mouth of HaShem they encamped.</b> The verse should have said 'at the mouth of HaShem the children of Israel journeyed and encamped,' not repeating 'at the mouth of HaShem they encamped.' But from what you know in the verse (Exodus 13) ״and HaShem went before them by day in a pillar of cloud and by night in a pillar of fire,״ the verse illuminates: 'at the mouth of HaShem they journeyed' — this is the attribute of judgment (din), and this is the sense of יסעו, for the journeying was for war; 'and at the mouth of HaShem they encamped' — this is the attribute of mercy, and this is the sense of יחנו, for every encampment is rest. And so it is written ״ויהי בנסוע הארון״ — 'and it came to pass when the ark journeyed' — ״קומה ה״ — 'Rise up, HaShem,' which is the attribute of judgment, and therefore it says קומה with a ה (heh) and did not say קום ה׳. And further it says ״וינוסו משנאיך מפניך״ — 'and let Your haters flee before You.' And at resting it says ״שובה ה״ — 'Return, HaShem' — from the language of (Isaiah 30) ״בשובה ונחת״ — 'in returning and rest,' for whenever Israel are gathered, thousands and myriads into a single fellowship, the attribute of mercy is with them. And these two attributes are included one within the other, and concerning them the prophet said (Jeremiah 2) ״זכרתי לך חסד נעוריך אהבת כלולותיך לכתך אחרי במדבר״ — 'I remember the lovingkindness of your youth, the love of your espousals, your going after Me in the wilderness.' And with them they were saved and their enemies were stricken: first in Egypt, as it is written (Hosea 13) ״ואנכי ה׳ אלהיך מארץ מצרים״, and written concerning the redemption from Egypt (Exodus 13) ״כי ביד חזקה הוציאנו ה׳ ממצרים״, and in the prayer of Moses (Exodus 32) ״אשר הוצאת מארץ מצרים בכח גדול וביד חזקה״; and afterward from Egypt to the Sea of Reeds, as it is written (Exodus 15) ״זה אלי ואנוהו״, and likewise (ibid.) ״ימינך ה׳ נאדרי בכח ימינך ה׳ תרעץ אויב״; and from the Sea of Reeds to Sinai, as it is written concerning the giving of the Torah (Deuteronomy 5) ״הן הראנו ה׳ אלהינו את כבודו ואת גדלו״; and from Sinai to the Tabernacle, as it is written (Exodus 40) ״וכסה הענן את אהל מועד וכבוד ה׳״ and it is written (ibid.) ״ולא יכול משה לבא אל אהל מועד כי שכן עליו הענן וכבוד ה׳״; and afterward to the Temple, which is called (Isaiah 64) ״בית קדשנו ותפארתנו״. And likewise in the future it is written (Isaiah 60) ״קומי אורי כי בא אורך וכבוד ה״ — 'Arise, shine, for your light has come, and the glory of HaShem.' And understand all this. And do not marvel at his saying 'the mouth of HaShem,' which is the attribute of mercy here, for since the attributes are included one within the other, each one is 'the mouth of HaShem' to the other. And understand this."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The author does not explicitly label a method-header for this comment; it is rendered as given without one. Verse citations normalized to book and chapter; chapter-only references retained as the author wrote them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:08.911342409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}